WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:08.210
There is nothing more annoying to a mentor
than somebody who is a total and I mean a

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:11.550
TOTAL askhole.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.820
Not the word you thought about before.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.890
. . I can't believe Pat said this on the title.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.359
No, no, askhole.

00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:18.929
It's an actual word, and you know what it
means?

00:00:18.929 --> 00:00:21.009
Let me tell you exactly what it means.

00:00:21.009 --> 00:00:28.369
An askhole is somebody who constantly asks
your advice, yet does the complete opposite

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:29.750
of what you tell them.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.930
You see, this is very important to me because
for many years, I'm a by-product of many different

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:35.930
mentors.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.260
And one of the things I had was, I do not
want to lose good mentors.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.340
I do not want to lose great advisers.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.400
I do not want to lose people that pour into
me regularly.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:51.150
And, I used to mentor this one person quite
a lot, and then one day, he and I had a conversation

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.210
together, and he said, "Hey Pat, I want to
be more accountable to you."

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.210
And I said, "What for?"

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.290
He said, "What do you mean?

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.700
I want to be more accountable to you."

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.120
I said, "What is your outcome of being accountable?"

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.470
So we can communicate more.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.620
I said, "For what?

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.820
What's your outcome on the business side,
not personal side.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.000
You can call me anything you want with my
family, with your family, friends, all this

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.220
other stuff because we have a relationship,
but I don't understand why in business you

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.290
want to be accountable to me."

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.360
He said, "Well, so you can give me direction."

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.810
I said, "Why would I give you any direction?"

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.700
He said, "Why wouldn't you give me direction?"

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.250
I said, "Why would I ever give you direction?"

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.250
And we went back and forth.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.670
I said, "Listen, you don't understand.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.479
You're a total askhole."

00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:27.000
And he said, "Pat, how could you say that
to me?"

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.650
I said, "I want you to take a quick pause
and go online and search that word."

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.000
And he went online and there's silence.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.170
And I said, "Are you reading it?"

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.490
He said, "I just read it."

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:41.750
I said, "Look, the last seven things, let
me remind you, the last seven conversations

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.180
we've had, that I've given you direction,
do you realize that you've done the complete

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.070
opposite of everything I told you the last
seven times?

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.590
The last seven times, you've done the opposite.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:56.060
I am no longer in a place in my life -- I
have three kids all under the age of five,

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.230
I run a company with a lot of employees, a
lot of agents, partners, vendors, I have commitments

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.479
to people that I'm doing things for.

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.060
I don't have time to mentor people who are
askholes."

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.060
And we went back and forth.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.690
I said, "So call me if you have family stuff
you want to talk to me about, because I care

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:15.000
for you, but on the business end, I just really
can't help you any more.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.000
I wish you all the best."

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.810
"I can't believe this is how it is, Pat."

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:19.980
I said, "No, no.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:25.500
You don't realize, there's a great thing,
when you find a mentor, who actually knows

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.700
what they're doing.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.310
They have put tens of thousands of hours into
their business of becoming a master.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.099
It is very difficult to find a great mentor.

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:41.510
When you do find a great mentor, that is teaching
you, be extremely coachable to them, especially

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:44.319
if it's somebody that you want their life,
their all-around life.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:49.390
If this is somebody that's willing to take
the time to pour into you, and teach you,

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:54.630
just make sure that when they do, you're learning
from them and you're implementing what they

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:59.410
are teaching you, because there's one thing
you've got to keep in mind.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:06.620
There's never, never, never, ever, ever, a
lack of supply of people who want to learn

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.970
from a mentor.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:15.060
But there is absolutely, absolutely a lack
of supply of great mentors.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:22.270
That is why those who end up finding a great
mentor have an edge over everybody else.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:27.320
Because it saves them tens of thousands of
hours of mistakes that they would have made.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:30.150
So my message to you is very simple.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.560
If you have a great mentor, who has the lifestyle
that you want, they're making the money you

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.879
want to make, they have a great personal life,
they have a good family life, they're raising

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:40.570
kids, they're doing things that they're growing.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.570
They're getting better.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:42.570
They're always in it.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.570
They're working.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:46.050
They're not just sitting on the sidelines
in retirement mode, kicking back.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.620
I'm talking, they're in the game.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:52.519
And they're willing to pour into you, be extremely
coachable to them.

00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:58.230
Do not be an askhole, until they decide to
move on and go mentor somebody else who is

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.069
willing to be coachable to them.

